# What does not belong in the package.
#
# `node_modules` is excluded: esbuild bundles `vscode-languageclient` and its
# own dependencies into `dist/extension.js`, so none of the 331 files those
# packages are made of need to ship separately. Before bundling, `vsce`
# shipped every one of them; now it ships one file.
# `src/` is excluded for the same reason: it is the bundle's input, not
# something the installed extension runs.
# `RELEASE.md` is the release *page*, written for somebody deciding whether to
# download this; the packaged `readme.md` is for somebody who already has it.
# Shipping both would put two overlapping introductions inside the extension.
#
# `scripts/` builds the icon and is not needed to run it. `sharp` is what does
# the rendering: it is a build tool with a large native binary per platform,
# installed on demand rather than declared, so `vsce` has no dev-dependency
# entry to prune it by and would ship every byte. Excluded by name because the
# only thing standing between it and the package is this line.
.vscode/**
.gitignore
install.ps1
RELEASE.md
PUBLISHING.md
DEVELOPING.md
scripts/**
src/**
node_modules/**
*.vsix
